statement:
Let m ∈ ℕ, n := m+1, U ⊆ ℝⁿ = Eucl n an arbitrary set, e_i := EuclideanSpace.single i 1, and let dx be Lebesgue measure (volume). Let X ∈ D_n(U) be integer multiplicity (IsIntegerMultiplicity X). Then there is u : ℝⁿ → ℝ such that:
(i) u(x) ∈ ℤ for Lebesgue-a.e. x ∈ ℝⁿ;
(ii) u is integrable on every compact K ⊆ U;
(iii) X(ω) = ∫_U u(x)·ω(x)(e_1,…,e_n) dx for every ω ∈ Dⁿ(U) (TestFormOn U n).
